{
  "description": "C2 runtime snapshot of public/, plus the C1 hub scripts and the C4 authoritative client (public/js/net-hub.js). Six lossless fighter atlases were added and the 240 pose PNGs were kept as unused sources. Startup preload is the six atlases plus stage 01 and stage 05 scenery (10 images). Gzip-9 uses mtime 0. Decoded cost is width * height * 4 and still counts the unused pose files on disk. The vendored SDK IIFE is copied into dist/ and is not part of this public tree. The banked HUD strings replaced the H3-C placeholder and grew the public tree by the text delta only. The crash guard (public/js/crash.js, loaded first, and the panel styles in index.html) added one critical script and its bytes. The server-restart resume retry (ZK-02) grew net-hub.js and the main.js HUD note by 6833 bytes. Controller support added public/js/gamepad.js (one more startup script) and the pad and keyboard menu code grew input.js and main.js. The Marina Anchor Relic report (hub SDK 0.6.4) grew hub-link.js and main.js by 3162 bytes, with no new file or request. The feedback window adapter (hub SDK 0.7.0) added public/js/feedback-link.js, one more startup script, which puts critical requests at the cap of 30, and with its main.js hooks grew the public tree by 14093 bytes. The gameplay improvement plan (readability pass, end-of-run summary and stage unlocks, synthesized music, and three sim batches) grew main.js, render.js, audio.js, sim.js and ai.js; its Progress module sits in audio.js so the page stays at 30 startup requests, and no audio file was added. Not reporting a stage-1 clear for a knocked-out player grew main.js by 1247 bytes. Raising Shadow Sproto and boss health grew sim.js by 91 bytes. Full-window fit, the shared menu options (MAIN MENU, RETURN TO BAR, CONTROLLER SETTINGS, FULL SCREEN) and the controller settings screen grew input.js, gamepad.js and main.js by 23863 bytes, with no new file or request. crossorigin=\"anonymous\" on the two Google Fonts links in index.html (hub SDK 0.7.2 draws page HTML into the feedback screenshot and needs it for the font) grew index.html by 48 bytes. Progress per hub account (hub SDK 0.8.0: the progress store and its wiring in audio.js, hub-link.js and main.js, free play split out as a device setting) grew the public tree by 9029 bytes, with no new file or request. Four seats (sim, protocol, lobby, HUD, relay) and the boss attack effects (four reused sheets in assets/fx/, 13,077 bytes, packed by tools/build-boss-fx.py, in the load plan and prefetched with the first stage) grew the public tree by 20930 bytes. The in-game effect drawing moved out of render.js into public/js/render-fx.js, which Render.enterStage loads after the title screen, so the title load shrank by 3734 bytes (tests/atlas-visual.cjs measured 1,568,951 transferred bytes against the 1,572,864 cap; main was at 1,572,685). Caps are unchanged: title 1.5 MiB, first stage 3 MiB, 30 critical requests, 10 MiB static. No CPU Sprotos: a seat nobody takes stays empty (sim seatIn/seatOut, protocol, lobby, HUD and the banked client), which grew the public tree by 2537 bytes and the title load by 2387 bytes, with no new file or request.",
